is friction the force acting on the earth is friction so yes. The third rule was are both

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:51.780
forces equal in size? Yes they are. The fourth rule was are the opposite in direction? Yes they

00:22:51.780 --> 00:22:56.960
are. And the fifth rule was do they act in a straight line? Yes they are. So this person

00:22:56.960 --> 00:23:02.600
running on the earth is an example of a Newton&#x27;s third law pair. Let&#x27;s look at another example.

00:23:03.620 --> 00:23:08.940
We have a book resting on a table and the question says do the following pair of forces adhere to

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:13.120
Newton&#x27;s third law? And the two forces are reaction force and weight of book. I&#x27;ll tell

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:17.080
you right now this violates rule number two for Newton&#x27;s third law because we have a reaction

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:25.190
force and a weight force. Those forces are not the same so Newton&#x27;s third law pair does not

00:23:25.190 --> 00:23:30.250
exist here. So let&#x27;s look at my notes on this. Rule number one was they act on two separate

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:35.490
bodies and there&#x27;s a book and a table fine. Rule number two was the forces must be the same.

00:23:35.830 --> 00:23:42.150
The force on the book is weight but the force on the table is the reaction force. So these two

00:23:42.150 --> 00:23:48.930
forces are not the same type of force. However they&#x27;re both equal in size they&#x27;re both opposite

00:23:48.930 --> 00:23:53.030
and they act in a straight line so we were nearly there but these forces do not adhere

00:23:53.030 --> 00:24:00.170
to Newton&#x27;s third law. Please can you head to your revision note template and write down the

