00:24:37.910 --> 00:24:42.930
into contact with. The first one we look at and we&#x27;ve seen a little bit already is the normal

00:24:42.930 --> 00:24:48.350
force and sometimes it&#x27;s called the reaction force. In IB physics it&#x27;s given the notation

00:24:48.350 --> 00:24:56.910
f sub score n. The definition of the normal force is the component of the contact force

00:24:57.470 --> 00:25:03.530
acting perpendicular to the surface that counters the body. We&#x27;ve already seen that when we

00:25:03.530 --> 00:25:07.230
considered the book resting on the table earlier. You can see that the normal force

00:25:07.230 --> 00:25:13.990
is acting perpendicular to the surface in contact and the weight force is causing that

00:25:15.030 --> 00:25:21.770
contact force. If we have somebody resting against a wall the normal force is perpendicular

00:25:22.620 --> 00:25:28.050
to the hard surface. If we consider a ball rolling down a hill the normal force is perpendicular

00:25:28.870 --> 00:25:34.990
to the hard surface. That&#x27;s the key point for reaction force or the normal force

00:25:34.990 --> 00:25:39.110
that it&#x27;s always acting perpendicular to the surface and contact.

00:25:40.070 --> 00:25:46.610
Next we&#x27;ll look at the frictional force and in IB physics notation is given f sub score f.

00:25:47.430 --> 00:25:55.250
The definition is the surface frictional force acting in a direction parallel to the surface

00:25:55.250 --> 00:26:00.970
of the plane contact between a body and surface. So you can see this frictional force here with

00:26:00.970 --> 00:26:06.390
the box being pushed along the surface. That frictional force is parallel to the surface

00:26:06.390 --> 00:26:12.030
of the plane contact and it&#x27;s in the opposite direction. So this box is moving that way

00:26:12.030 --> 00:26:18.850
so the frictional force is moving this way. Look at the car. The car is moving this way

00:26:19.310 --> 00:26:24.730
so the frictional force is moving that way and it is in parallel to the contact surface.

00:26:25.830 --> 00:26:30.070
There are two different types of friction that you should be aware of.

