want an extra tutorial on this so I&#x27;ve added an extra tutorial on static and dynamic friction

00:26:44.430 --> 00:26:49.130
for you below just to delve into that in a little bit more detail. The next contact force we&#x27;ll look

00:26:49.130 --> 00:26:56.630
at is elastic force and in IB physics it&#x27;s given the notation f underscore h. The definition of the

00:26:56.630 --> 00:27:03.990
elastic force is the elastic force exerted by a material when it is stretched or compressed

00:27:04.410 --> 00:27:14.010
and tries to return to its original shape. This is all about Hooke&#x27;s law is fh is equal to minus kx.

00:27:14.710 --> 00:27:19.290
So when you&#x27;re discussing elastic force you&#x27;re inevitably going to be looking at Hooke&#x27;s law.

00:27:19.910 --> 00:27:25.550
You&#x27;ve probably seen Hooke&#x27;s law in relation to a spring where it&#x27;s being compressed or stretched

00:27:25.550 --> 00:27:33.930
and that&#x27;s where this all comes into play. The next contact force is called viscous drag force

00:27:34.750 --> 00:27:42.870
and it is given the notation f underscore d. The definition is the resistive force exerted by a fluid

00:27:43.750 --> 00:27:48.990
on an object moving through it. The example we have here is a ball bearing

00:27:49.830 --> 00:27:55.990
moving downwards through castor oil as a result of its weight and there&#x27;s a force acting backwards

00:27:55.990 --> 00:28:02.190
resisting its motion which is drag a bit like friction and it&#x27;s eventually going to balance

00:28:02.190 --> 00:28:08.250
out and cause a constant speed here. The key point of this is the viscous drag force is greater in

00:28:08.250 --> 00:28:15.250
thicker fluids so if you have a fluid that&#x27;s got a high viscosity like honey castor oil then

00:28:15.250 --> 00:28:20.690
that drag force that viscous drag force is going to be greater. There is a formula

00:28:21.630 --> 00:28:27.010
for a small sphere falling through a fluid and this formula for viscous drag force

00:28:27.010 --> 00:28:33.350
six pi nu r v where nu is a fluid viscosity and that would be given to you.

00:28:33.770 --> 00:28:41.370
