So it really depends on what situation you&#x27;re looking at. The definition of gravitational

00:30:27.910 --> 00:30:31.970
force, and we go into this in much more detail later on in the IB physics course,

00:30:32.050 --> 00:30:39.670
is a force that attracts two objects with mass towards each other and the key point here is

00:30:39.670 --> 00:30:46.410
all objects with mass exert gravitational forces. The larger the mass the stronger the gravitational

00:30:46.410 --> 00:30:53.490
pull. The next non-contact force is electric force. It has the notation f underscore e.

