momentum and impulse for collisions and explosions, one-dimensional for SL and two-dimensional for HL.

00:33:15.430 --> 00:33:22.930
Okay let&#x27;s define linear momentum. Linear momentum is defined as the product of mass and velocity of

00:33:22.930 --> 00:33:27.730
an object and in fact it&#x27;s almost always acceptable just to define it as the formula.

00:33:27.730 --> 00:33:34.190
Momentum is given the notation p equals mv. You&#x27;ll notice there&#x27;s arrows above p and v,

00:33:34.330 --> 00:33:40.330
that&#x27;s just to denote that momentum and velocity are vectors so linear momentum is a vector

00:33:40.330 --> 00:33:46.530
quantity. It does matter what direction we look at for momentum. The units of momentum,

00:33:46.930 --> 00:33:50.690
you can actually use two different units, you can use kilograms meters per second squared

00:33:51.430 --> 00:33:56.710
and that&#x27;s because the units of mass is kilograms and the units of velocity is

00:33:56.710 --> 00:34:02.490
meters per second squared so you put them together and you get kilograms meters per second squared.

00:34:02.750 --> 00:34:10.490
But there&#x27;s also the opportunity to use newton seconds. Why can we use newton seconds? Well let&#x27;s

00:34:10.490 --> 00:34:16.630
consider the formula for force which we know of course has units of newtons, the formula is mA.

00:34:17.270 --> 00:34:23.850
So the units of newtons can also be written as kilograms meters per second squared and these

00:34:23.850 --> 00:34:31.690
are all SI units, they&#x27;re all fundamental units. We&#x27;re nearly at the stage where we have the same

00:34:31.690 --> 00:34:38.330
units as momentum but this s to the minus two is an issue. So if we take the units here

00:34:39.090 --> 00:34:46.410
and multiply it by s then what we get is kgms to the minus one and that is the equivalent of

00:34:47.230 --> 00:34:54.450
newtons seconds. So newton seconds is the same as kilograms meters per second and they can both be

00:34:54.450 --> 00:35:01.010
used as units for linear momentum. When an object is traveling along, here&#x27;s my car,

00:35:01.770 --> 00:35:08.310
it&#x27;s terrible isn&#x27;t it? It has mass, it has velocity, you can work out what the momentum is,

00:35:08.770 --> 00:35:16.030
easy. We&#x27;re kind of interested more in momentum when we look at things crashing or colliding

00:35:16.030 --> 00:35:23.150
or exploding. We&#x27;re looking at the interaction of this car doing something and that&#x27;s where

00:35:23.150 --> 00:35:29.390
the conservation of momentum comes in. The law of conservation of momentum states that

00:35:30.050 --> 00:35:36.370
during any interaction where no external force is at, the total linear momentum is conserved

00:35:36.370 --> 00:35:42.330
in any specified direction. So what does that mean? It means the car that we looked at earlier

00:35:42.330 --> 00:35:49.470
crashes then the momentum before that crash is the same as the momentum afterwards as long as

00:35:49.470 --> 00:35:55.330
there&#x27;s no external forces acting and that looks mathematically like the total momentum before a

00:35:55.330 --> 00:36:01.910
collision is equal to the total momentum after a collision and you can see they&#x27;re both vector

00:36:01.910 --> 00:36:08.810
quantities so direction does matter. The main thing that you&#x27;ll be asked to do in an IB

00:36:08.810 --> 00:36:13.950
physics exam is solve a problem to find out what the velocity of an object is after a collision

00:36:13.950 --> 00:36:20.530
or what the total mass of an object is using this idea of the conservation of momentum and

00:36:20.530 --> 00:36:25.870
there&#x27;s a set of five rules I would use to make sure you answer those questions perfectly.

00:36:26.570 --> 00:36:31.950
The first rule is the clue that you&#x27;re using momentum and the conservation of momentum.

00:36:31.950 --> 00:36:38.630
The clue is you&#x27;ll see the words collision, explosion or you might even see the word

00:36:38.630 --> 00:36:45.070
momentum which would be the biggest clue. Then you draw a diagram on the left hand side you draw

00:36:45.070 --> 00:36:49.890
a diagram of the situation before the collision and on the right hand side you draw a diagram

00:36:50.410 --> 00:36:56.210
of the situation after the collision. Number three, rule number three is to choose a direction as

00:36:56.210 --> 00:37:02.550
positive. Number four is to apply momentum to each body before and after the collision and number

00:37:02.550 --> 00:37:07.970
five is to remember that momentum before equals momentum after. Now does that sound complicated?

