00:47:23.630 --> 00:47:31.550
force on the car lessens. If you jump and bend your knees by bending your knees you&#x27;re increasing

00:47:31.550 --> 00:47:36.730
the time it takes to stop and you&#x27;re decreasing the force on your knees thus saving your joints

00:47:37.530 --> 00:47:44.010
and a tennis racket what you actually want to do is increase the force on that ball on your

00:47:44.010 --> 00:47:48.350
tennis racket so you want to decrease the amount of time it takes to change the momentum of the

00:47:48.350 --> 00:47:55.950
ball which means you want a very tight string so you want tight strings on your tennis racket to

00:47:55.950 --> 00:48:02.250
increase the force that the ball is released with. So impulse begins to allow us to explain

00:48:02.250 --> 00:48:08.670
real life situations. If I can just direct your attention up here for the moment I think it&#x27;s

00:48:08.670 --> 00:48:13.110
pretty easy to use this formula there&#x27;s not much in it and it should be relatively simple for you

00:48:13.110 --> 00:48:24.490
that is it&#x27;s simple if the force is constant it&#x27;s simple because it&#x27;s just a formula you pop in the

