00:53:22.790 --> 00:53:28.530
With that knowledge we can actually do a little bit of vector subtraction to find out

00:53:28.530 --> 00:53:33.550
what the direction of acceleration is for an object that&#x27;s undergoing circular motion.

00:53:34.750 --> 00:53:41.010
We know that acceleration is defined as the rate of change of velocity so we would like to find the

00:53:41.010 --> 00:53:49.170
change in velocity of this satellite that&#x27;s shown around the earth and the change in

00:53:49.170 --> 00:53:56.830
