00:53:56.830 --> 00:54:03.870
you the trick on how to subtract vectors it&#x27;s the final velocity plus minus the initial velocity.

00:54:04.990 --> 00:54:14.930
So let&#x27;s take that down to here. We want to subtract v1 here from v2 here and to do that we add

00:54:15.550 --> 00:54:23.690
v2 plus minus v1. Minus v1 now v1 isn&#x27;t going in that direction so minus v1 is going in that

00:54:23.690 --> 00:54:30.810
direction. We&#x27;re going to add vectors v2 and minus v1 tip to tail and that will give you

00:54:30.810 --> 00:54:39.630
the resultant vector in this direction here. So the vector direction of the change in velocity

00:54:40.450 --> 00:54:48.550
or the acceleration is in this direction here. No matter what stage you do that around

00:54:49.510 --> 00:54:57.310
the circular motion you always have the change in velocity vector directed towards the center.

00:54:57.490 --> 00:55:03.090
The acceleration vector is always directed towards the center no matter where you do

