00:56:23.990 --> 00:56:31.150
Let&#x27;s start very simply. We really want to understand radians and why they&#x27;re used in physics.

00:56:31.670 --> 00:56:34.890
Okay, radians are often used because they&#x27;re multiples of pi

00:56:34.890 --> 00:56:39.750
which is a natural number and it&#x27;s a natural unit for trigonometric functions.

00:56:41.450 --> 00:56:49.030
Physicists prefer radians. It links everything in much better and the angle in radians is defined

00:56:49.030 --> 00:56:54.830
as the arc length divided by the radius. So you can see the arc length is here

00:56:55.970 --> 00:57:02.390
divided by the radius which is here and if we compare it with degrees, degrees is based

00:57:02.390 --> 00:57:09.750
on dividing a circle into 360 equal parts whereas radians is only based on the radius of the circle.

00:57:10.450 --> 00:57:17.230
It is important you understand that both degrees and radians can be used and understand that

00:57:17.230 --> 00:57:26.190
90 degrees is equal to pi over 2 radians, 180 degrees is equal to pi radians,

00:57:26.810 --> 00:57:33.990
360 degrees is equal to 2 pi radians and so on. You should be able to convert between the two.

00:57:34.770 --> 00:57:42.730
I think it&#x27;s now time to define angular displacement. Angle displacement is defined as the angle in

00:57:42.730 --> 00:57:49.470
radians or degrees through which a point has been rotated about a specific axis. You can see on the

00:57:49.470 --> 00:57:56.190
diagram here the angular displacement is the angle through which a point has been rotated

00:57:56.190 --> 00:58:02.510
and it&#x27;s to do with the arc length and the radius. Let&#x27;s have a look at linear velocity. Let&#x27;s have

00:58:02.510 --> 00:58:09.570
a think about how fast something is moving around a circle. Linear velocity or tangential velocity

00:58:09.570 --> 00:58:15.930
is the velocity of a point on a rotating object. So if we think about a satellite orbiting earth

00:58:15.930 --> 00:58:25.290
like we did had earlier then the tangential velocity is this. Okay that&#x27;s a terrible diagram

00:58:25.290 --> 00:58:31.270
but there we go and the formula for linear velocity is 2 pi r over t. You will recognize

00:58:31.270 --> 00:58:38.720
2 pi r as their circumference and the circumference is equal to a distance.

00:58:40.680 --> 00:58:47.660
So the linear velocity is equal to distance over time which is 2 pi r over t. R is of course the

00:58:47.660 --> 00:58:53.700
radius of the point and the units of linear velocity are meters per second also written

00:58:53.700 --> 00:59:01.290
like this. If you consider a wheel and we have two points, a red and a blue point,

00:59:01.490 --> 00:59:09.670
those points are placed on the wheel. The red point has a smaller radius than the blue point

00:59:10.190 --> 00:59:17.810
and if we consider the equation v equals 2 pi r over t then the red point has a smaller radius

00:59:17.810 --> 00:59:22.690
which means it has a smaller linear velocity than the blue point. So when you&#x27;re considering

00:59:22.690 --> 00:59:27.570
linear velocity the radius may be smaller for something which means that the linear velocity

00:59:27.570 --> 00:59:34.950
is smaller. However let&#x27;s now look at angular velocity. Angular velocity is given the symbol

00:59:34.950 --> 00:59:40.230
omega. Angular velocity is a rate of change of angular displacement with respect to time

00:59:40.230 --> 00:59:46.090
and if you remember earlier we had angular displacement as this angle here. So angular

00:59:46.090 --> 00:59:52.710
velocity is how quickly does this angle change? It&#x27;s the rate of change of angular displacement.

00:59:54.710 --> 00:59:59.850
Theta is the angular displacement, t is the time taken and the units of angular velocity

00:59:59.850 --> 01:00:09.640
is rads per second or radians per second. Looks like that. If you consider this red point and

01:00:09.640 --> 01:00:15.000
the blue point on the wheel again, the rate at which the angular displacement changes

01:00:15.000 --> 01:00:33.260
for the red dot and the blue dot is exactly the same. So even though v red has a smaller

01:00:33.260 --> 01:00:42.000
linear speed and angular velocity and we can do that using this relationship v equals omega r.

01:00:42.920 --> 01:00:49.900
Let&#x27;s remind ourselves of the equations. Linear speed is equal to v equals 2 pi over t. The units

01:00:49.900 --> 01:00:57.340
are meters per second. Angular velocity is omega equals theta over t and the units are radians

01:00:57.340 --> 01:01:03.020
per second and we can link linear speed and angular velocity using this relationship.

01:01:04.360 --> 01:01:07.860
Do you remember when we were discussing the satellite going around in a circle

01:01:08.460 --> 01:01:15.680
and we analyzed the velocity vectors to find the change in velocity and what we found was

01:01:15.680 --> 01:01:21.900
that the acceleration was always directed towards the center of the circle. We found that out

